                <head>300. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Executive Order 10945, “Administration of the Export Control Act of 1949,” was
                    signed by the President on May 24, 1961, establishing the Export Control Review
                    Board, a Cabinet committee consisting of the Secretaries of Commerce (Chairman),
                    State, and Defense. (Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>,
                    June 12, 1961, pages 934-935; 26 <hi rendition="#italic">Federal</hi> Register
                    4487) Its purpose was to assure high-level consideration of trade control
                    policies and actions and to obtain agreed action among Departments chiefly
                    concerned with advising the Secretary of Commerce, in accordance with the Export
                    Control Act of 1949, as amended. (50 USC App. 2021, 2024)</p>
            </div>
